WEBVTT

NOTE tts=synthetic

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.267
When should a breaker front head be replaced?

2
00:00:03.267 --> 00:00:09.533
Cracks mostly start around the key holes, the tie-rod holes and the corners.

3
00:00:09.533 --> 00:00:15.633
A worn or oval seat lets even a new bushing move or turn; the tool works at an angle.

4
00:00:15.633 --> 00:00:20.500
Oval holes let the key move, take shock loads and break often.

5
00:00:20.500 --> 00:00:23.733
Replace bushings and tools in time.

6
00:00:23.733 --> 00:00:28.033
Working with worn bushings passes the load straight to the head.
